Two firms sell an identical product. Inverse demand is P = 178 − Q, where Q is total output. Firm L has a constant marginal cost of 18 and firm F has a constant marginal cost of 2; neither has fixed costs. Firm L chooses its quantity first; firm F observes it and then chooses its own quantity to maximize profit. First: if firm L produced 134 units, how many units would firm F produce? Reply with only the number.